[
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "h2",
    "text": "31.5 Electric",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 944,
    "anchor": "electric",
    "section": "31.5",
    "locator": "electric:B001"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "Electric is a software electric piano developed in collaboration with Applied Acoustics Systems. It is based on the classic instruments of the seventies; each component has been modeled using cutting edge physical modeling technology to provide realistic and lively sounds.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 956,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B002"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "Physical modeling uses the laws of physics to reproduce the behavior of an object. In other words, Electric solves, in real time, mathematical equations describing how its different components function. No sampling or wavetables are used in Electric; the sound is calculated in real time by the CPU according to the values of each parameter. Electric is more than a simple recreation of vintage instruments; its parameters can be tweaked to values not possible with the real instruments to get some truly amazing new sounds that still retain a warm acoustic quality.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 956,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B003"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "h3",
    "text": "31.5.1 Architecture and Interface",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.1 Architecture and Interface",
        "html_line": 956,
        "anchor": "architecture-and-interface-2",
        "section": "31.5.1"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 956,
    "anchor": "architecture-and-interface-2",
    "section": "31.5.1",
    "locator": "electric:B004"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The mechanism of the electric piano is actually quite simple. A note played on the keyboard activates a hammer that hits a fork. The sound of that fork is then amplified by a magnetic coil pickup and sent to the output, very much like an electric guitar. The fork is made of two parts, called the tine bar and tone bar. The tine bar is where the hammer hits the fork while the tone bar is a tuned metal resonator, sized appropriately to produce the correct pitch. Once the fork is activated, it will continue to resonate on its own for a long time. But releasing the key applies a damper to the fork, which mutes it more quickly.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.1 Architecture and Interface",
        "html_line": 956,
        "anchor": "architecture-and-interface-2",
        "section": "31.5.1"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 956,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B005"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Electric interface is divided into four main sections: Hammer, Fork, Damper/Pickup, which contain parameters pertaining to the instrument’s tone and sound; and the Global section which contains parameters that affect overall behavior and performance, such as pitch bend and polyphony.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.1 Architecture and Interface",
        "html_line": 956,
        "anchor": "architecture-and-interface-2",
        "section": "31.5.1"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 956,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B006"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "You can click on the individual sections to reveal all of their associated parameters, or you can click on the Hammer, Fork, or Damper/Pickup icons to toggle between those respective sections.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.1 Architecture and Interface",
        "html_line": 956,
        "anchor": "architecture-and-interface-2",
        "section": "31.5.1"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 956,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B007"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "h3",
    "text": "31.5.2 Hammer Section",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.2 Hammer Section",
        "html_line": 968,
        "anchor": "hammer-section",
        "section": "31.5.2"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 968,
    "anchor": "hammer-section",
    "section": "31.5.2",
    "locator": "electric:B008"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Hammer section contains the parameters related to the physical properties of the hammer itself, as well as how it’s affected by your playing.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.2 Hammer Section",
        "html_line": 968,
        "anchor": "hammer-section",
        "section": "31.5.2"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 980,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B009"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Stiffness knob adjusts the hardness of the hammer’s striking area. Higher values simulate a harder surface, which results in a brighter sound. Lower values mean a softer surface and a more mellow sound. Stiffness can also be modified by velocity and note pitch via the Vel and Key sliders in the bottom half of the display.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.2 Hammer Section",
        "html_line": 968,
        "anchor": "hammer-section",
        "section": "31.5.2"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 980,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B010"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Noise knob adjusts the amount of impact noise caused by the hammer striking the fork. In the Noise section in the bottom half of the display, the Pitch slider sets the center frequency of the noise pitch, while the Decay slider adjusts how long it takes for the noise to fade to silence. The Key slider controls how much the noise volume is determined by note pitch.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.2 Hammer Section",
        "html_line": 968,
        "anchor": "hammer-section",
        "section": "31.5.2"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 980,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B011"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Force section adjusts the intensity of the hammer’s impact on the fork. Low Amount values simulate a soft impact while high values result in a hard impact. Force can also be modified by velocity and note pitch, via the Vel and Key sliders.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.2 Hammer Section",
        "html_line": 968,
        "anchor": "hammer-section",
        "section": "31.5.2"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 980,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B012"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "h3",
    "text": "31.5.3 Fork Section",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.3 Fork Section",
        "html_line": 980,
        "anchor": "fork-section",
        "section": "31.5.3"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 980,
    "anchor": "fork-section",
    "section": "31.5.3",
    "locator": "electric:B013"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Fork section contains knobs for both Tine and Tone parameters, which are the heart of Electric’s sound generating mechanism.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.3 Fork Section",
        "html_line": 980,
        "anchor": "fork-section",
        "section": "31.5.3"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 992,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B014"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "Tine controls the portion of the fork that is directly struck by the hammer.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.3 Fork Section",
        "html_line": 980,
        "anchor": "fork-section",
        "section": "31.5.3"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 992,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B015"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Color slider controls the relative amplitude of high and low partials in the tine’s spectrum. Low values result in lower harmonics, while higher values result in higher harmonics.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.3 Fork Section",
        "html_line": 980,
        "anchor": "fork-section",
        "section": "31.5.3"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 992,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B016"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Decay knob adjusts how long it takes the tine’s sound to fade out while a note is held. The volume level of the tine can be modulated by note pitch via the Key slider.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.3 Fork Section",
        "html_line": 980,
        "anchor": "fork-section",
        "section": "31.5.3"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 992,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B017"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "Tone controls the secondary resonance of the fork.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.3 Fork Section",
        "html_line": 980,
        "anchor": "fork-section",
        "section": "31.5.3"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 992,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B018"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Release slider applies to both Tine and Tone, and controls the decay time of the fork’s sound after a key is released. The Decay parameter works in the same way as in the Tine subsection.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.3 Fork Section",
        "html_line": 980,
        "anchor": "fork-section",
        "section": "31.5.3"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 992,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B019"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "h3",
    "text": "31.5.4 Damper/Pickup Section",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.4 Damper/Pickup Section",
        "html_line": 992,
        "anchor": "damperpickup-section",
        "section": "31.5.4"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 992,
    "anchor": "damperpickup-section",
    "section": "31.5.4",
    "locator": "electric:B020"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "h4",
    "text": "31.5.4.1 Pickup Parameters",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.4 Damper/Pickup Section",
        "html_line": 992,
        "anchor": "damperpickup-section",
        "section": "31.5.4"
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "text": "31.5.4.1 Pickup Parameters",
        "html_line": 1004,
        "anchor": "pickup-parameters",
        "section": "31.5.4.1"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 1004,
    "anchor": "pickup-parameters",
    "section": "31.5.4.1",
    "locator": "electric:B021"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "In Electric, the Pickup simulates the behavior of the magnetic coil pickup that amplifies the sound of the resonating fork.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.4 Damper/Pickup Section",
        "html_line": 992,
        "anchor": "damperpickup-section",
        "section": "31.5.4"
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "text": "31.5.4.1 Pickup Parameters",
        "html_line": 1004,
        "anchor": "pickup-parameters",
        "section": "31.5.4.1"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 1004,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B022"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Symmetry knob and Distance slider adjust the physical location of the pickup in relation to the tine. Symmetry simulates the vertical position of the pickup. At 50%, the pickup is directly in front of the tine, which results in a brighter sound. Lower amounts move the pickup below the tine, while higher amounts move it above the tine. Distance controls how far the pickup is from the tine. Higher amounts increase the distance, while lower amounts move the pickup closer. Note that the sound becomes more overdriven as the pickup approaches the tine.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.4 Damper/Pickup Section",
        "html_line": 992,
        "anchor": "damperpickup-section",
        "section": "31.5.4"
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "text": "31.5.4.1 Pickup Parameters",
        "html_line": 1004,
        "anchor": "pickup-parameters",
        "section": "31.5.4.1"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 1004,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B023"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Type R and W buttons switch between two different types of pickups. In the R position, Electric simulates electro-dynamic pickups, while W is based on an electro-static model.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.4 Damper/Pickup Section",
        "html_line": 992,
        "anchor": "damperpickup-section",
        "section": "31.5.4"
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "text": "31.5.4.1 Pickup Parameters",
        "html_line": 1004,
        "anchor": "pickup-parameters",
        "section": "31.5.4.1"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 1004,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B024"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Input slider is used to adjust the amount of the fork’s signal that is fed to the pickup, which in turn affects the amount of distortion applied to the overall signal. The Output slider controls the amount of signal output by the pickup section. Different combinations of these two parameters can yield very different results. For example, a low amount of input with a high amount of output will produce a cleaner sound than a high input with a low output. The output level can be further modulated by note pitch via the Key slider.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.4 Damper/Pickup Section",
        "html_line": 992,
        "anchor": "damperpickup-section",
        "section": "31.5.4"
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "text": "31.5.4.1 Pickup Parameters",
        "html_line": 1004,
        "anchor": "pickup-parameters",
        "section": "31.5.4.1"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 1004,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B025"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "h4",
    "text": "31.5.4.2 Damper Parameters",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.4 Damper/Pickup Section",
        "html_line": 992,
        "anchor": "damperpickup-section",
        "section": "31.5.4"
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "text": "31.5.4.2 Damper Parameters",
        "html_line": 1004,
        "anchor": "damper-parameters",
        "section": "31.5.4.2"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 1004,
    "anchor": "damper-parameters",
    "section": "31.5.4.2",
    "locator": "electric:B026"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The metal forks in an electric piano are designed to sustain for a long time when a key is held. The mechanism that regulates this sustain is called the damper. When a key is pressed, that note’s damper is moved away from its fork. When the key is released, the damper is applied to the fork again to stop it from vibrating. But the dampers themselves make a small amount of sound, both when they are applied and when they are released. The Damper parameters simulate this characteristic noise.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.4 Damper/Pickup Section",
        "html_line": 992,
        "anchor": "damperpickup-section",
        "section": "31.5.4"
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "text": "31.5.4.2 Damper Parameters",
        "html_line": 1004,
        "anchor": "damper-parameters",
        "section": "31.5.4.2"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 1004,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B027"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Tone slider adjusts the stiffness of the dampers. Lower values simulate soft dampers, which produces a mellower sound. Higher values increase the hardness of the dampers, producing a brighter sound. The overall amount of damper noise is adjusted with the Level slider.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.4 Damper/Pickup Section",
        "html_line": 992,
        "anchor": "damperpickup-section",
        "section": "31.5.4"
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "text": "31.5.4.2 Damper Parameters",
        "html_line": 1004,
        "anchor": "damper-parameters",
        "section": "31.5.4.2"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 1004,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B028"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "p",
    "text": "The Att/Rel slider adjusts whether or not damper noise is present when the dampers are applied to the fork or when they are released. At -100, damper noise will only be heard during the note’s attack phase. At 100, the noise is present only during the release phase. In the center, an equal amount of noise will be present during both attack and release.",
    "heading_context": [
      {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "31.5 Electric",
        "html_line": 944,
        "anchor": "electric",
        "section": "31.5"
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "text": "31.5.4 Damper/Pickup Section",
        "html_line": 992,
        "anchor": "damperpickup-section",
        "section": "31.5.4"
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "text": "31.5.4.2 Damper Parameters",
        "html_line": 1004,
        "anchor": "damper-parameters",
        "section": "31.5.4.2"
      }
    ],
    "html_line": 1004,
    "anchor": null,
    "section": null,
    "locator": "electric:B029"
  },
  {
    "device": "electric",
    "kind": "h3",
    "text": "31.5.5 Global Section",
    "heading_context": [
      {
